radonc — Radon-equivalent cyclomatic complexity

The cyclomatic-complexity counting rules in this crate are a port of the
Python `radon` library (https://github.com/rubik/radon), specifically its
`radon/complexity.py` module. The rule set — if/elif counting, loop and
try/else, assert non-recursion, match minus wildcard, boolop operands-1,
ternary, comprehension generators+ifs, lambda +0 body walked, nested
function and class body exclusion — is reproduced faithfully from radon
6.0.1.

